---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import TableOfContents from '../components/TableOfContents.astro';
import ResumeReading from '../components/ResumeReading.astro';
import { ACTS, READING_PATHS, readingMinutes } from '../lib/book';
import '../styles/book.css';
const chapters = await getCollection('chapters', ({ data }) => !data.draft);
const count = chapters.filter(c => c.data.chapterNumber != null).length;
const start = chapters.find(c => c.id === 'prologue');
const sampler = ['prologue', '10-the-information-physical-duality', '20-how-we-change-the-world'].map(id => chapters.find(c => c.id === id)!);
const samplerMinutes = sampler.reduce((total, chapter) => total + readingMinutes(chapter.body), 0);
const paths = READING_PATHS.map(path => ({
  ...path,
  entries: path.chapters.map(number => {
    const chapter = chapters.find(c => c.data.chapterNumber === number);
    if (!chapter) throw new Error(`Missing chapter ${number} in reading path: ${path.id}`);
    return chapter;
  }),
}));
---
<BaseLayout title="The book" cinematic>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main class="book-page" id="main-content">
    <header>
      <p class="book-kicker">Three acts · {count} chapters · Working drafts</p>
      <h1 class="book-title">Follow the thread.</h1>
      <p class="book-lead">Life doesn’t always make sense. Even when it should. Follow that question through wanting, knowledge, culture, society, technology, and the living world we belong to.</p>
      <div class="book-actions"><a class="book-button" href="/chapters/prologue">Begin the book · about {readingMinutes(start?.body)} min →</a><ResumeReading /></div>
      <p class="book-small">Reading estimates cover the prose. Pause as long as you like for the optional practices.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="book-section" aria-labelledby="route-heading">
      <h2 id="route-heading">Why this order?</h2>
      <ol class="book-acts">
        {ACTS.map(act => <li><a class="book-act" href={`/acts/${act.key}`} style={`--act-color: ${act.color}`}>
          <span class="book-act__num" aria-hidden="true">{act.roman}</span><div><h3>{act.name}</h3><p>{act.premise}</p><small>{act.alias} · Act {act.roman} →</small></div>
        </a></li>)}
      </ol>
      <div class="book-aside"><p>Something matters to a living being. Distinctions make a world possible to understand and act in. Shared descriptions become knowledge, tools, and institutions, which change the conditions of living. Each act follows the consequences of the one before it.</p><p>The acts build on one another. You can also enter through a question that is already yours.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="book-section" aria-labelledby="paths-heading">
      <h2 id="paths-heading">A few other doors.</h2>
      <div class="book-aside"><h3>Try a short sample · about {samplerMinutes} minutes</h3><p>Begin with the book’s question, see how information changes the physical world, then ask what makes collective change worth making.</p><ol>{sampler.map(chapter => <li><a href={`/chapters/${chapter.id}`}>{chapter.data.title}</a></li>)}</ol></div>
      <div class="book-paths">{paths.map(path => <article id={`path-${path.id}`} aria-labelledby={`path-title-${path.id}`}><h3 id={`path-title-${path.id}`}>{path.title}</h3><p>{path.description}</p><ol>{path.entries.map(chapter => <li><a href={`/chapters/${chapter.id}`}>{chapter.data.chapterNumber}. {chapter.data.title}</a></li>)}</ol></article>)}</div>
    </section>
    <section class="book-section" aria-labelledby="contents-heading">
      <h2 id="contents-heading">The whole book.</h2>
      <p>The prologue is the suggested beginning. The preface is an optional origin story. Every chapter is a working draft, open to correction.</p>
      <TableOfContents chapters={chapters} />
    </section>
    <section class="book-section">
      <h2>A way to read.</h2>
      <p>Read a scene. Notice the claim it invites. Try another explanation. Take a practice into your own week, if it fits. Your disagreement is useful material.</p>
      <details><summary>How certain is any of this?</summary><p>Examples you can inspect, research findings, and philosophical proposals carry different kinds of support. The chapters mark those differences and link to selected sources. A convincing story can still be wrong.</p></details>
      <a class="book-link" href="/practice">Find a small experiment →</a>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
